{{!--
    The Thread editor. ("node" in code, "Thread" to the reader.)

    Four questions, in the order a GM answers them: what it is, how it advances,
    whether it is open, and what concluding it does. Each is a section with a
    heading and one sentence saying what it decides — the M7 pass, and the same
    treatment the ⓘ badges got in M5.5. Before it, this screen was a run of
    fields in schema order with nothing saying which two mattered.

    The two gates share a section on purpose. M6 keeps them independent in the
    code — a reveal does not pay off a requirement — but to the reader they
    answer one question, which is *why will this not open*, and answering it in
    two places three sections apart is how a GM ends up looking for a third gate
    that does not exist.

    Outcomes are one row per Force on the Plot rather than a repeating widget:
    the set is fixed by the roster, so there is nothing to add or remove. A row
    left at zero with nothing written is not saved.

    Prerequisites are chips plus a picker, so a Plot with twenty Threads does not
    become twenty checkboxes.
--}}

<section class="rsr-form-section">
    <h3>{{localize "RSR.editor.secWhat"}}</h3>
    <p class="rsr-form-lead">{{localize "RSR.editor.secThreadWhatLead"}}</p>
    <p class="rsr-form-note">
        {{localize "RSR.editor.threadOn"}} <strong>{{editor.plotName}}</strong>
    </p>

    <div class="rsr-form-row">
        <label for="rsr-f-name">{{localize "RSR.editor.name"}}</label>
        <input type="text" id="rsr-f-name" name="name" value="{{editor.draft.name}}">
    </div>
    <div class="rsr-form-row is-tall">
        <label for="rsr-f-description">{{localize "RSR.editor.description"}}</label>
        <textarea id="rsr-f-description" name="description" rows="3">{{editor.draft.description}}</textarea>
    </div>
</section>

{{!--
    How it advances.

    THIS SECTION ASKS ONLY WHAT THE MODE CAN ANSWER. It used to ask everything of
    everybody: a Narrative Thread, which tracks nothing at all, was asked for a
    threshold, a segment count and a direction to read them in — three fields it
    would never look at, and no way for a GM to tell a field that is ignored from
    one they forgot to fill in.

    `editor.shape` is the answer, built from the ONE table in logic/progress.mjs
    that the arithmetic reads too, so the form and the maths cannot drift. The
    mode select carries `data-reshapes`, which harvests and re-renders on change —
    so nothing typed is lost when the section rebuilds around a new answer.

    The Consequence is the second track, and it is not a mode: every mode but
    Narrative may carry one, and a Thread with the toggle off is the Thread it
    always was.
--}}
<section class="rsr-form-section">
    <h3>{{localize "RSR.editor.secThreadAdvance"}}</h3>
    <p class="rsr-form-lead">{{localize "RSR.editor.secThreadAdvanceLead"}}</p>

    <div class="rsr-form-row">
        <label for="rsr-f-mode">{{localize "RSR.editor.mode"}}</label>
        <select id="rsr-f-mode" name="mode" data-reshapes>
            {{#each editor.modes}}
            <option value="{{this.value}}"{{#if this.selected}} selected{{/if}}>
                {{#if this.isInherit}}
                {{localize this.label mode=(localize @root.editor.inheritedMode)}}
                {{else}}
                {{localize this.label}}
                {{/if}}
            </option>
            {{/each}}
        </select>
    </div>

    {{!-- What this mode actually counts. It matters most on Narrative, where the
          rows below are absent and the section would otherwise read as a form
          that broke rather than as an answer. --}}
    <p class="rsr-form-note">{{localize editor.modeLead}}</p>

    {{!-- One question per row. These were a single row with the second label
          living inside the first row's inline span, where the CSS draws it small
          and grey — a second question wearing the clothes of an annotation on
          the first. --}}
    {{#if editor.shape.threshold}}
    <div class="rsr-form-row">
        <label for="rsr-f-threshold">{{localize "RSR.editor.threshold"}}</label>
        <span class="rsr-form-inline">
            <input type="number" id="rsr-f-threshold" name="threshold" min="1"
                   value="{{editor.draft.threshold}}">
            <i class="fa-regular fa-circle-question rsr-info" data-tooltip-class="rsr-tip"
               data-tooltip="{{localize 'RSR.editor.thresholdHint'}}"></i>
        </span>
    </div>
    {{/if}}

    {{#if editor.shape.segments}}
    <div class="rsr-form-row">
        <label for="rsr-f-segments">{{localize "RSR.editor.segments"}}</label>
        <span class="rsr-form-inline">
            <input type="number" id="rsr-f-segments" name="segments" min="1"
                   value="{{editor.draft.segments}}">
            <i class="fa-regular fa-circle-question rsr-info" data-tooltip-class="rsr-tip"
               data-tooltip="{{localize 'RSR.editor.segmentsHint'}}"></i>
        </span>
    </div>
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- Sits under the number it is about: it decides which way that number is
          read, not what it is. It no longer carries a scope note in its label —
          the row is simply absent on the one mode with no number to run either
          way, which says the same thing without asking the reader to hold it. --}}
    {{#if editor.shape.countdown}}
    <div class="rsr-form-row">
        <label for="rsr-f-countdown">{{localize "RSR.editor.countdown"}}</label>
        <span class="rsr-form-check">
            <input type="checkbox" id="rsr-f-countdown" name="countdown"{{#if editor.draft.countdown}} checked{{/if}}>
            <i class="fa-regular fa-circle-question rsr-info" data-tooltip-class="rsr-tip"
               data-tooltip="{{localize 'RSR.editor.countdownHint'}}"></i>
        </span>
    </div>
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- The Consequence. A subsection rather than one more row, because turning
          it on adds a whole second reading to the row this Thread draws, and a
          checkbox in a run of numbers would not say so. --}}
    {{#if editor.shape.consequence}}
    <div class="rsr-form-sub">
        <h4>{{localize "RSR.editor.consequence"}}</h4>
        <p class="rsr-form-lead">{{localize "RSR.editor.consequenceLead"}}</p>

        <div class="rsr-form-row">
            <label for="rsr-f-consequence-on">{{localize "RSR.editor.consequenceOn"}}</label>
            <span class="rsr-form-check">
                <input type="checkbox" id="rsr-f-consequence-on" name="consequenceOn" data-reshapes{{#if editor.draft.consequenceOn}} checked{{/if}}>
                <i class="fa-regular fa-circle-question rsr-info" data-tooltip-class="rsr-tip"
                   data-tooltip="{{localize 'RSR.editor.consequenceHint'}}"></i>
            </span>
        </div>

        {{#if editor.draft.consequenceOn}}
        <div class="rsr-form-row">
            <label for="rsr-f-consequence-size">{{localize "RSR.editor.consequenceSize"}}</label>
            <span class="rsr-form-inline">
                <input type="number" id="rsr-f-consequence-size" name="consequenceSize" min="1"
                       value="{{editor.draft.consequenceSize}}">
                <i class="fa-regular fa-circle-question rsr-info" data-tooltip-class="rsr-tip"
                   data-tooltip="{{localize 'RSR.editor.consequenceSizeHint'}}"></i>
            </span>
        </div>

        {{!-- Contested alone. Two sides racing each other rarely go wrong the
              same way at the same rate, but one complication mounting over the
              whole contest is just as ordinary a shape — so the GM says which. --}}
        {{#if editor.shape.perForce}}
        <div class="rsr-form-row">
            <label for="rsr-f-consequence-per-force">{{localize "RSR.editor.consequencePerForce"}}</label>
            <span class="rsr-form-check">
                <input type="checkbox" id="rsr-f-consequence-per-force" name="consequencePerForce"{{#if editor.draft.consequencePerForce}} checked{{/if}}>
                <i class="fa-regular fa-circle-question rsr-info" data-tooltip-class="rsr-tip"
                   data-tooltip="{{localize 'RSR.editor.consequencePerForceHint'}}"></i>
            </span>
        </div>
        {{/if}}
        {{/if}}
    </div>
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- The Expiration Clock, and it is OUTSIDE every shape branch on purpose.
          A deadline is not a way of advancing, it is a way of running out — the
          Narrative Thread that tracks nothing at all can be given three cycles
          exactly as readily as the Clock can, which is why it is absent from
          MODE_SHAPE and present here whatever the picker says. --}}
    <div class="rsr-form-sub">
        <h4>{{localize "RSR.editor.expiry"}}</h4>
        <p class="rsr-form-lead">{{localize "RSR.editor.expiryLead"}}</p>

        <div class="rsr-form-row">
            <label for="rsr-f-expiry-on">{{localize "RSR.editor.expiryOn"}}</label>
            <span class="rsr-form-check">
                <input type="checkbox" id="rsr-f-expiry-on" name="expiryOn" data-reshapes{{#if editor.draft.expiryOn}} checked{{/if}}>
                <i class="fa-regular fa-circle-question rsr-info" data-tooltip-class="rsr-tip"
                   data-tooltip="{{localize 'RSR.editor.expiryHint'}}"></i>
            </span>
        </div>

        {{#if editor.draft.expiryOn}}
        <div class="rsr-form-row">
            <label for="rsr-f-expiry-size">{{localize "RSR.editor.expirySize"}}</label>
            <span class="rsr-form-inline">
                <input type="number" id="rsr-f-expiry-size" name="expirySize" min="1"
                       value="{{editor.draft.expirySize}}">
                <i class="fa-regular fa-circle-question rsr-info" data-tooltip-class="rsr-tip"
                   data-tooltip="{{localize 'RSR.editor.expirySizeHint'}}"></i>
            </span>
        </div>

        {{!-- Which clock takes the time away. The Plot's own is offered only
              while that Plot is keeping one — a setting that quietly does
              nothing is worse than an absent one. --}}
        <div class="rsr-form-row">
            <label for="rsr-f-expiry-clock">{{localize "RSR.editor.expiryClock"}}</label>
            <span class="rsr-form-inline">
                <select id="rsr-f-expiry-clock" name="expiryClock" data-reshapes>
                    {{#each editor.expiryClocks}}
                    <option value="{{this.value}}"{{#if this.selected}} selected{{/if}}>{{localize this.label}}</option>
                    {{/each}}
                </select>
                <i class="fa-regular fa-circle-question rsr-info" data-tooltip-class="rsr-tip"
                   data-tooltip="{{localize 'RSR.editor.expiryClockHint'}}"></i>
            </span>
        </div>

        {{!-- The clock is running on nothing: this Thread rides its Plot's own
              cycle and the Plot is no longer keeping one. Said rather than
              silently repaired, because the fix is a decision — move the Thread
              to the world's clock, or the Plot back onto its own. --}}
        {{#if editor.expiryStranded}}
        <p class="rsr-form-note is-condition">{{localize "RSR.editor.expiryStranded"}}</p>
        {{/if}}

        <div class="rsr-form-row">
            <label for="rsr-f-expiry-label">{{localize "RSR.editor.expiryLabel"}}</label>
            <span class="rsr-form-inline">
                <input type="text" id="rsr-f-expiry-label" name="expiryLabel"
                       value="{{editor.draft.expiryLabel}}"
                       placeholder="{{localize editor.expiryPlaceholder}}">
                <i class="fa-regular fa-circle-question rsr-info" data-tooltip-class="rsr-tip"
                   data-tooltip="{{localize 'RSR.editor.expiryLabelHint'}}"></i>
            </span>
        </div>
        {{/if}}
    </div>
</section>

{{!-- Both gates, in one place, because they answer one question. --}}
<section class="rsr-form-section">
    <h3>{{localize "RSR.editor.secThreadOpen"}}</h3>
    <p class="rsr-form-lead">{{localize "RSR.editor.secThreadOpenLead"}}</p>

    <div class="rsr-form-row">
        <label for="rsr-f-status">{{localize "RSR.editor.status"}}</label>
        <span class="rsr-form-inline">
            <select id="rsr-f-status" name="status">
                {{#each editor.statuses}}
                <option value="{{this.value}}"{{#if this.selected}} selected{{/if}}>{{localize this.label}}</option>
                {{/each}}
            </select>
            <i class="fa-regular fa-circle-question rsr-info" data-tooltip-class="rsr-tip"
               data-tooltip="{{localize 'RSR.editor.statusHint'}}"></i>
        </span>
    </div>

    <div class="rsr-form-row is-stacked">
        <label>
            {{localize "RSR.editor.prereqs"}}
            <i class="fa-regular fa-circle-question rsr-info" data-tooltip-class="rsr-tip"
               data-tooltip="{{localize 'RSR.editor.prereqsHint'}}"></i>
        </label>
        <span class="rsr-form-stack">
            {{#if editor.prereqs.length}}
            <span class="rsr-chip-row">
                {{#each editor.prereqs}}
                <span class="rsr-edit-chip">
                    <span>{{this.name}}</span>
                    <button type="button" class="rsr-icon-btn rsr-icon-tiny" data-action="removePrereq"
                            data-thread-id="{{this.id}}" data-tooltip="{{localize 'RSR.editor.removePrereq'}}">
                        <i class="fa-solid fa-xmark" inert></i>
                    </button>
                </span>
                {{/each}}
            </span>
            {{else}}
            <span class="rsr-form-note">{{localize "RSR.editor.noPrereqs"}}</span>
            {{/if}}

            {{#if editor.availablePrereqs.length}}
            <span class="rsr-form-add">
                <select id="rsr-pick-prereq" name="pick-prereq">
                    <option value="">{{localize "RSR.editor.pickThread"}}</option>
                    {{#each editor.availablePrereqs}}
                    <option value="{{this.id}}">{{this.name}}</option>
                    {{/each}}
                </select>
                <button type="button" class="rsr-btn" data-action="addPrereq">
                    <i class="fa-solid fa-plus" inert></i>
                    <span>{{localize "RSR.editor.addPrereq"}}</span>
                </button>
            </span>
            {{/if}}
        </span>
    </div>
</section>

{{!-- What concluding this Thread does to the Plot, per Force. --}}
<section class="rsr-form-section">
    <h3>
        {{localize "RSR.editor.outcomes"}}
        <i class="fa-regular fa-circle-question rsr-info" data-tooltip-class="rsr-tip"
           data-tooltip="{{localize 'RSR.editor.outcomesHint'}}"></i>
    </h3>
    <p class="rsr-form-lead">{{localize "RSR.editor.outcomesLead"}}</p>

    {{#if editor.outcomes.length}}
    <div class="rsr-outcome-head">
        <span>{{localize "RSR.editor.outcomeWho"}}</span>
        <span>{{localize "RSR.editor.outcomeMoves"}}</span>
        <span>{{localize "RSR.editor.outcomeSays"}}</span>
    </div>
    {{#each editor.outcomes}}
    <div class="rsr-outcome-row">
        <span class="rsr-outcome-force">{{this.name}}</span>
        <input type="number" id="rsr-oc-delta-{{this.forceId}}" class="rsr-outcome-delta"
               data-row-group="outcomes" data-row-key="{{this.forceId}}" data-row-field="delta"
               value="{{this.delta}}"
               aria-label="{{localize 'RSR.editor.outcomeMoves'}}">
        <input type="text" id="rsr-oc-note-{{this.forceId}}"
               data-row-group="outcomes" data-row-key="{{this.forceId}}" data-row-field="note"
               value="{{this.note}}" placeholder="{{localize 'RSR.editor.outcomeNotePlaceholder'}}"
               aria-label="{{localize 'RSR.editor.outcomeSays'}}">
    </div>
    {{/each}}
    {{else}}
    <p class="rsr-form-note">{{localize "RSR.editor.noForcesOnPlot"}}</p>
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- The one ending with no Force behind it. Two plain named controls rather
          than a data-row-group row: the repeating rows above are keyed by Force
          id and swept by it in three places, and a row in that list standing for
          nobody would have to survive all three. --}}
    {{#if editor.consequenceOutcome}}
    <div class="rsr-outcome-row is-consequence">
        <span class="rsr-outcome-force">
            <i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation" inert></i>
            {{localize "RSR.thread.consequence"}}
        </span>
        <input type="number" id="rsr-f-consequence-delta" class="rsr-outcome-delta"
               name="consequenceDelta" value="{{editor.consequenceOutcome.delta}}"
               aria-label="{{localize 'RSR.editor.outcomeMoves'}}">
        <input type="text" id="rsr-f-consequence-note" name="consequenceNote"
               value="{{editor.consequenceOutcome.note}}"
               placeholder="{{localize 'RSR.editor.consequenceNotePlaceholder'}}"
               aria-label="{{localize 'RSR.editor.outcomeSays'}}">
    </div>
    {{/if}}
</section>
